cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the works listed in docs/REFERENCES.md."
title: "Ego2Humanoid: From Egocentric RGB Video to Physically Validated Humanoid Manipulation"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: kevinlisun
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kevinlisun/ego2humanoid"
abstract: >-
  Ego2Humanoid turns one egocentric RGB clip of a person performing a pick-and-place task into an
  action-controlled MuJoCo rollout of a Unitree G1 humanoid with Dex3-1 or Sharpa Wave hands. RGB-only
  perception (monocular geometry, 3D hands, vision-to-tactile contact, open-vocabulary objects, image-to-3D
  meshes) feeds a kinematic retargeting stage with closed-loop grasp correction; acceptance requires
  independent pick-place events on the achieved object state.
keywords:
  - humanoid robotics
  - dexterous manipulation
  - egocentric video
  - motion retargeting
  - real-to-sim
  - MuJoCo
